       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "Q8BLY2"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Catalyzes the attachment of threonine to tRNA(Thr) in a two-step reaction: threonine is first activated by ATP to form Thr-AMP and then transferred to the acceptor end of tRNA(Thr). Also edits incorrectly charged tRNA(Thr) via its editing domain, at the post-transfer stage"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
   "reaction": {
    "name": "tRNA(Thr) + L-threonine + ATP = L-threonyl-tRNA(Thr) + AMP + diphosphate + H(+)",
